{
  "dom_id": "step-q334970",
  "name": "Question 1",
  "problem": "Given that $J(t)={\\int }_{0}^{1}(3x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t))^{2}\\,\\text{d}x,$ calculate ${J}^{′}(t)$ for $t\\in R$ by differentiating under the integral sign.\n\n${J}^{′}(t)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡t(\\,$\n{{field-1}}$)$",
  "worked_solution": "Suppose $f(x,t)$ is continuous on $R=[a,b]\\times [c,d]$ and $\\frac{∂f}{∂t}$ exists and is continuous on $R.$ Then, the function\n\n$$\nF(t)={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x,t)\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\nis differentiable on $(c,d),$ and\n\n$$\n{F}^{′}(t)=\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x,t)\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{a}^{b}\\frac{∂f}{∂t}(x,t)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nThis is known as differentiating under the integral sign.\n\nWe wish to compute ${J}^{′}(t),$ where\n\n$$\nJ(t)={\\int }_{0}^{1}(3x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t))^{2}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating under the integral sign, we get\n\n$$\n{J}^{′}(t)={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{∂}{∂t}[(3x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t))^{2}]\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nNext, let's compute the partial derivative with respect to $t$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂t}[(3x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t))^{2}] & =2(3x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t))\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂t}(3x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)) \\\\  & =2(3x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t))\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡(t) \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)(3x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this back into our integral, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{J}^{′}(t) & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)(3x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t))\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t){\\int }_{0}^{1}(3x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t))\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, let's evaluate the remaining integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(3x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t))\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}3x\\,\\text{d}x-{\\int }_{0}^{1}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3{x}^{2}}{2}{|}_{0}^{1}-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)\\cdot x{|}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{J}^{′}(t) & =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)(\\frac{3}{2}-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(t)(3-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(t)).\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
